Explain Idea
The main idea for this project is to amend the original YOLO real-time object detection systems with focus on Biker hand signal detection for autonomous driving systems. The trained network will go beyond simple object identification and attempt to recognize the cyclists’ intention. The result would be a more ethical autonomous driving system that provides a safer road condition for both driver and cyclist. 


What type of computer vision problem is this?

The Binary Object classification, tracking (continuous motion), localization and instance segmentation

Binary Object classification/tracking to detect the cyclists in motion as in complicated real world traffic scenarios, there could be multiple cyclists heading different directions in various states(static/in motion). 

Localization and Instance segmentation enable more detailed understanding of the circumstances. For instance, localization can help to detect the number of cyclists and use this later to determine their direction of travel, distance from the driver, and intention from their hand gesture. 

This will be supervised learning with all the images labelled. The first stage will be to identify cyclists from the images and the second stage is to detect their turn signallings with their hand gestures. 

What type of data will you need? How are you going to access or collect this data?

We will need images of various ages, genders, ethnic groups of cyclists traveling in different times, terrains, weathers, traffic conditions and costumes in both images and videos.

